  "Number": 18,
  "Question": "The arithmetic mean (average) of the first \\(n\\) positive integers is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac n2\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{n^2}{2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(n\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{n-1}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{n+1}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Let \\(n\\) be a positive integer and let \\(S=1+2+\\cdots+n\\). To find the mean, first find this total. Write a second copy in reverse order and add corresponding terms. Each integer \\(k\\), for \\(1\\le k\\le n\\), is paired with \\(n+1-k\\), so every pair sums to \\(n+1\\). There are \\(n\\) such pairs, giving\n\\[\n2S=n(n+1),\\qquad S=\\frac{n(n+1)}2.\n\\]\nThe mean is the total divided by the number of terms. Since \\(n>0\\),\n\\[\n\\frac Sn=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2n}=\\boxed{\\frac{n+1}{2}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
